Read a custom shade colour of black as a colour

The reader turned a custom shade into no shade when the colour was pure
black. The test covers six inputs: the menu bar, the sliders, the check
marks, the menu stripe, the combination button and the sorted header.

The dialog stores a black colour as the text #000000, because the colour
button starts at black and the writer always stores seven characters.
The next read answers none, the dialog shows None, and the choice of the
user is gone. A colour one step from black, #010101, paints 14352 pixels
of the menu bar, while black paints none at all.

Drop the test. A custom shade now uses the colour that the file names.
The bare name custom names no colour, so the input keeps its shipped
colour, which is black.

Only a file that holds a custom black changes, and it changes to the
colour that it holds.

The change sits on the branch work/config-io of the local tree, as commit 9 of 18.
A new merge request on system/qtcurve takes that branch.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

